<BlogPost
  title="Gravitational Waves: The Historic Discovery That Changed Physics"
  description="Learn about the groundbreaking 2015 detection of gravitational waves, what they are, and why this discovery revolutionized our understanding of the universe."
  publishDate="2024-01-20"
  author="mitija"
  readTime="9 min read"
  keywords="gravitational waves, LIGO, black holes, spacetime ripples, Einstein prediction"
>
  <p>
    On September 14, 2015, humanity detected something Einstein predicted a century earlier but thought we'd never
    observe: gravitational waves. This discovery opened an entirely new way of observing the universe and confirmed
    one of the most remarkable predictions of general relativity.
  </p>

  <h2>What Are Gravitational Waves?</h2>
  <p>
    Gravitational waves are ripples in the fabric of spacetime itself, caused by some of the universe's most
    violent and energetic processes. When massive objects accelerate, they create distortions that propagate
    outward at the speed of light, stretching and compressing space as they pass.
  </p>

